WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/vehicles/components/vehicle-detail/ChargingTelemetrySection.tsx — a PURE presentational leaf fed a
  `chargingTelemetry: ChargingTelemetry | null | undefined` prop by its parent (the Vehicle Detail page) and the
  distance/speed preference from `useUnits()`. It renders:
    GlassPanel(p-6) → header[ <Zap/> (neon-green) + {t('vehicles.detail.chargingTelemetry','Charging Telemetry')} ]
                    → grid-cols-2 / sm:3 / lg:4 of eight <MetricCard>s (muted 10px label, bold text-primary value, a
                      tinted icon chip), each with a per-field em-dash fallback:
        1 Charger Power  (green , Zap)            : charger_power_w != null ? `${fmtNumber(v)} kW`  : '—'
        2 Voltage        (cyan  , Activity)       : charger_voltage != null ? `${fmtNumber(v)} V`   : '—'
        3 Current        (purple, Activity)       : charger_actual_current != null ? `${fmtNumber(v)} A` : '—'
        4 Energy Added   (green , BatteryCharging): charge_energy_added_wh != null ? `${fmtNumber(v)} kWh` : '—'
        5 Charging State (cyan  , Battery)        : charging_state ?? '—'
        6 Battery Level  (green , Battery)        : battery_level != null ? `${fmtNumber(v)}%` : '—'
        7 Charge Rate    (cyan  , Activity)       : range_added_meters_per_hour != null ? formatSpeed(v / 3600) : '—'
        8 Range Added    (purple, Zap)            : range_added_meters != null ? formatDistance(v) : '—'
                    OR (chargingTelemetry == null) → <EmptyState Zap> {t('vehicles.detail.noChargingTelemetry',
                      'No charging telemetry available')}.
  Data sources (prompt): useTranslation + useUnits. No data-fetching hook — it is a presentational leaf; the only
  branches are the per-field em-dash fallbacks + the null→EmptyState branch (all reproduced verbatim). fmtNumber default
  = 2-decimal locale format, safeNumber coerces non-finite → 0. formatDistance = DEFAULT_PRECISION.distance(1dp), SI
  metres ÷1000 (km) / ÷1609.344 (mi); formatSpeed = DEFAULT_PRECISION.speed(0dp), SI m/s ×3600÷1000 (km/h) /
  ×3600÷1609.344 (mph). Charge Rate divides metres/hour by 3600 to an SI m/s before formatSpeed (reproduced exactly).

